<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mieszko II Lambert</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 990–<a href="/years/1034">1034</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Mieszko II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mieszko II Lambert was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> from 1025 to 1031 and again ruled from 1032 until his death in 1034, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-i-the-brave">Bolesław I the Brave</a>. His reign saw attacks by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus</a>, revolts by his brothers, the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lusatia">Lusatia</a> and the royal crown, and the collapse of royal authority. After his death a pagan reaction and a Bohemian invasion devastated the country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mieszko-ii-lambert.jpg" alt="Mieszko II Lambert" width="320" height="375" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Darstellung_Mieszkos_und_Mathildes_von_Schwaben.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
